  "Notes": [
    {
      "Text": "libtiff security update",
      "Title": "Synopsis",
      "Type": "General"
    },
    {
      "Text": "An update for libtiff is now available for openEuler-22.03-LTS-SP4",
      "Title": "Summary",
      "Type": "General"
    },
    {
      "Text": "This  provides support for the Tag Image File Format (TIFF), a widely used format for storing image data. The latest version of the TIFF specification is available on-line in several different formats.And contains command-line programs for manipulating TIFF format image files using the libtiff library.\n\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\nAn issue in libtiff allows an attacker to execute arbitrary code via the process_command_opts() function in tools/tiffcrop.c. The vulnerability is classified as CWE-94 (Code Injection), where the product constructs all or part of a code segment using externally-influenced input from an upstream component, but it does not neutralize or incorrectly neutralizes special elements that could modify the syntax or behavior of the intended code segment.(CVE-2026-52490)\n\nAn issue in libtiff 85f2ac8e0b01cb7db2bbecf4a3b891bdbef67938 allows an attacker to execute arbitrary code via the libtiff/tools/thumbnail.c: main() component(CVE-2026-52491)\n\nAn integer overflow in the libtiff rgb2ycbcr utility's cvtRaster() function when computing strip buffer sizes can result in an undersized heap allocation and subsequent heap-based buffer overflow during YCbCr conversion of a crafted TIFF image.(CVE-2026-52492)",
      "Title": "Description",
      "Type": "General"
    },
    {
      "Text": "An update for libtiff is now available for openEuler-22.03-LTS-SP4.\n\nopenEuler Security has rated this update as having a security impact of critical. A Common Vunlnerability Scoring System(CVSS)base score,which gives a detailed severity rating, is available for each vulnerability from the CVElink(s) in the References section.",
      "Title": "Topic",
      "Type": "General"
    },
    {
      "Text": "Critical",
      "Title": "Severity",
      "Type": "General"
    },
    {
      "Text": "libtiff",
      "Title": "Affected Component",
      "Type": "General"
    }
  ],
